# File spec for ./test.rhai — the shipped, currently UNCALLED script lane of
# `agent package test`: the Rust @TestHandler::run_test_inner duplicates the context+install
# chain as an inline snippet and never imports this module. Script semantics only; the clap
# surface, the engine, the TestSet/Test model, the verdict and the exit ladder belong to
# /agent/src/package/test.sdd and /agent/src/testing/*.sdd — named, never restated.
# Calibrated on ./build.sdd (packages-lane shape) and ./../lib/secret_dockerconfigjson.sdd
# (Rhai-module shape).

Spec: PackagesTest

Platform: Rhai script (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine / locked rhai)

Purpose:
  Stage-rehearse install on whatever engine imports it: stage the package sources into
    `{args.temp}` via @build::build, retarget `args.package_dir` at the staged tree, seed
    `args.tag` from `instance.status.tag` else the literal `0.0.1`, then run the shared
    @ctx::run + @install::run chain — the type-agnostic superset of the Rust test engine's
    inline install snippet. No importer exists in the repository today: the module ships
    orphaned (Tasks holds the seam decision).
  Complete file structure: three top-level @import lines (`build`, `context` as ctx,
    `install`) and one @fn definition (@run) — importing the module runs those three imports
    and defines the fn, with no other top-level effect.

Exposes:
  @run(instance, args) — the module's sole @fn, called as `test::run(instance, args)`; the
    same composable signature lane as the @ctx::run/@install::run calls it chains. Nothing in
    the repo (Rust, Rhai, product or test) imports this module, so nothing reaches it.
  Import contract: `import "test"` names this file only for resolver sets built with
    `{script_dir}/packages` (the build/update/validate Rust lanes); none of them imports `test`.

Accepts:
  @instance — a map or registered instance readable at `.status` and `.status.tag` (the reads
    are guarded for `()`; a non-map @instance would raise on the first property access).
  @args — the caller's map, mutated in place: keys read `temp` (log text, then @build::build),
    `namespace` and `instance` (log texts, both passed to callees); keys written before the
    chain `package_dir` := `args.temp` and `tag` := status tag or `0.0.1`.
  @build::build additionally reads `source` and `temp` (./build.sdd); @ctx::run and
    @install::run read further keys from the same map per their own modules. No existence,
    type or completeness preflight of any key or path here.

Returns:
  @run — the value of the trailing @install::run call, with no pinned meaning and no consumer.
    The file mints no verdict, no assert row, no tally and no summary.

Raises:
  Zero local @throw, zero try/catch — every callee failure propagates raw as an interpreter
    error; the exit lane would be the importing Rust arm's (`Rhai script error:` text).
  At module evaluation, before @run exists: the three bare imports are strict — a
    module-not-found on any aborts the whole import; notably the `agent package test` mock
    engine's resolver set ({package_dir}/scripts, config_dir, {script_dir}/{type},
    {script_dir}/lib) carries no `{script_dir}/packages`, so `import "build"` dies first and
    this module cannot load there at all (Tasks). The core @import_run debug-skip posture
    belongs to other shims, not to these bare imports.
  @build::build legs fire between the first log and the rewrites: staging and manifest throws
    owned by ./build.sdd (among them `{source}/package.yaml doesnt exist`).
  Missing-key shape errors: an absent key reads as @(); a JSON-injected engine-style args map
    without `source`/`temp` dies inside @build::build's path concat as a function-call error,
    never a fallback (./build.sdd posture).

Handles:
  `instance.status` or `.status.tag` absent — the two `!= ()` guards short-circuit before the
    nested read and the seed `0.0.1` is assigned; an empty `status {}` map (the test engine's
    virtual instance mock shape) takes the seed leg.
  Nothing else defensively: no empty/missing checks on args, no callee return inspection.

Must:
  Run @run in this exact order: @log_info `Building to ${args.temp}` → @build::build(@args) →
    `args.package_dir = args.temp` → tag assignment via the guard expression → @log_info
    `Generating context for ${args.namespace} ${args.instance}` → @ctx::run(@instance, @args) →
    @log_info `Installing ${args.namespace} ${args.instance}` → @install::run(@instance,
    @context). Exactly those three log texts, at those three positions.
  Call @build::build, never @build::run — staging only, so nothing lists, pushes, signs or
    @prints in this module; the tag rewrite sits AFTER the staging leg, so a status tag can
    never reach it (@build reads no tag in any case — ./build.sdd).
  Retarget install by mutating the shared map: `package_dir := args.temp` lands before
    @ctx::run, and the ctx/install lanes read package_dir from that map, installing from the
    staged tree instead of the source package directory; the caller's @resolver_path list is a
    separate Rust-built collection this assignment never touches.
  Keep the seed tag the literal `0.0.1` — a different seed from the `0.1.0` @build::run and the
    Rust @build_test_args carry (Tasks).
  Stay type-agnostic: no `service`/`system`/`tenant` branch or name here; the `context`/`install`
    aliases resolve to whichever type directory the importing engine's resolvers carry, so one
    module serves all three package types.
  Keep the engine surface consumed here to @log_info (core-registered tracing `info` sink — not
    stdout; this file has no @print), the three bare @imports, property/index reads, `!=`
    against `()` and backtick interpolation; fs, yaml, registry and cluster contact live
    exclusively in the callee modules.
  Consume no Test/TestSet document and no created-object sink: the TestSet/Test model, mock
    injection, assert evaluation and verdict aggregation are owned by /agent/src/testing/handler.sdd
    and /agent/src/package/test.sdd — a crashing @install::run would propagate to the
    importer untouched, which is where (never, today) it would be folded into a failed
    `execution` assert.

Must not:
  Produce a summary line, a JUnit file or a @common::Error::TestFailure — that contract is
    /agent/src/package/test.sdd's and is unreached by this module even in a failing chain.
  Read or write the filesystem, contact a registry or cluster, or mutate @instance — @args is
    the only object this file writes.

Depends on:
  ./build.rhai (./build.sdd) — imported as `build`; sole use is the @build staging leg.
  ./../../service/context.rhai, ./../../system/context.rhai, ./../../tenant/context.rhai —
    imported as `ctx`, one per caller resolver set; no same-basename specs exist yet.
  ./../../service/install.rhai, ./../../system/install.rhai, ./../../tenant/install.rhai —
    imported as `install`; run(instance, context) is the terminal call; no same-basename specs.
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script::new_mock and friends: which engine can even resolve the
    three imports.
  /agent/src/testing/handler.sdd — the real consumer of this file's context+install chain (as an
    inline snippet) and its would-be caller.

References:
  /agent/src/package/test.sdd — the Rust lane this script was presumed to feed: @run_test_inner
    evaluates its own five-line context+install snippet against @build_test_args keys, with no
    build leg, no rewrites and no `import "test"` — the presumed seam does not exist (Tasks).
  /agent/tests/rhai_build.rs — shows a test harness CAN build a `{base}/scripts/packages`
    resolver set, yet imports only `build`; `test` is imported nowhere.

Tasks:
  [?] Seam is dead code: nothing repo-wide imports `"test"`, and the test engine cannot — the
    mock resolvers lack `{script_dir}/packages` and @run_test_inner inlines the chain instead.
    Decide: route run_test_inner (and a future build-staged lane) through `import_run("test")`,
    or delete this file.
  [?] Args contract if wired: @build_test_args injects namespace/instance/dirs/tag/
    controller_values and none of `source`/`temp`/`registry` that @build::build needs — the
    first leg would crash even after fixing resolvers. Decide the injected args shape (and the
    mock-OCI story around a staging-only build).
  [?] Seed divergence `0.0.1` (here) vs `0.1.0` (@build::run seed and Rust @build_test_args tag).
    Decide the single seed.
  [?] `package_dir → temp` retarget while the caller resolver list keeps the ORIGINAL
    `{package_dir}/scripts`: freeze as intended staged-tree rehearsal or pair the two.
  [ ] Zero coverage: no /agent/tests/rhai_*.rs imports or runs this module (no `import "test"`
    anywhere in ./../../tests). When the seam decision lands, cover the scenarios below from a
    packages-resolver Rhai lane; until then no scenario is executable.

Done when:
  The seam `[?]` is decided (wired-and-scenario-tested, or the file deleted), and
    `cargo test -p agent` plus `specdd lint` stay green.

Scenario: staged rehearsal installs from the temp tree
  Given a resolver set carrying `packages` plus one type directory, an args map with a valid
    `source`/`temp`, and an instance whose `status.tag` is `2.3.4`
  When @run(instance, args) runs
  Then the order is log, @build::build, `package_dir = temp`, `tag = 2.3.4`, @ctx::run,
    log, @install::run(@instance, @context) — and no registry call is made (staging only)
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: statusless instance seeds the tag
  Given `instance.status` is `()` or an empty map
  Then the guards read no deeper, `args.tag` is the literal `0.0.1` before @ctx::run, and the
    chain proceeds
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: staging failure aborts before any rewrite
  Given @build::build raising (e.g. the missing-`package.yaml` throw of ./build.sdd)
  Then `args.package_dir` and `args.tag` keep their caller values, no further log line prints,
    and the context/install modules are never reached beyond their already-run imports
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: import from the package-test mock engine dies at evaluation
  Given the `agent package test` mock-engine resolver set
  When any script attempts `import "test"`
  Then the bare `import "build"` aborts the import itself as module-not-found — the
    `{script_dir}/packages` dir is absent from the set and bare imports never debug-skip
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  engine surface consumed: `log_info` only (three calls) + bare `import` × 3;
  arg writes verbatim: `args.package_dir = args.temp;` and
  `args.tag = if instance.status != () && instance.status.tag != () {instance.status.tag} else {"0.0.1"};`
